# commit-conventions

- Commit messages in **English**.
- Use Conventional Commits prefixes:
  - `feat:` — new feature or user-facing capability
  - `fix:` — bug fix
  - `chore:` — tooling, deps, seeds, config, docs that are not a product feature
  - Also allowed when needed: `docs:`, `refactor:`, `test:`, `style:`, `perf:`, `ci:`
- Format: `type: short description` (imperative, lowercase after the colon, no trailing period)
- Examples:
  - `feat: add auth login endpoint`
  - `fix: reject inactive membership on guard`
  - `chore: add role and demo user seeds`
- Keep subject to one line; add a blank line + body only when needed.
- Never commit `.env` or secrets.

$END$
